# Ignore all markdown files except README.md
*.md
!README.md
!**/README.md

# Compiler caches. Belt and braces: the scripts point these at out/ (already ignored),
# but a stray TORCHINDUCTOR_CACHE_DIR or a new script must not be able to commit them.
.inductor_cache/
.triton_cache/
**/.inductor_cache/
**/.triton_cache/

# Small build artefacts that every box has to hold an IDENTICAL copy of, and that
# `*.pt` above would otherwise swallow. About 4.4 MB in total.
#   perms/           vocabulary permutations. A factorised head is fitted to one
#                    specific assignment, so a box without it silently trains the
#                    token-id control instead of the arm you asked for.
#   tokenizer_131k/  the V=131072 tokenizer. Rebuilding one is a BPE training run,
#                    and two boxes that rebuilt separately are not the same tokenizer.
# Directory negations come first: git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, and tokenizer_131k/ is excluded by name above.
!perms/
!perms/**
!tokenizer_131k/
!tokenizer_131k/**

# tokenizer/ is NOT tracked. It was, and its tokenizer.pkl flip-flopped between the real
# 412 KB V=32768 file and a 1.9 KB V=265 byte-level stub across five commits, because
# anything that writes into ./tokenizer gets committed along with the next change. A run
# against the stub does not fail: base_train prints "Vocab size: 265", pads to 320 and
# trains to completion, so a whole sweep can produce bpb numbers that compare with
# nothing. Keep the real tokenizer outside the repo (~/.cache/nanochat/tokenizer) or on
# the box's own volume, and pass it with --tokenizer-dir.
# NOTE: research_sweep.sh trains a NEW tokenizer when tokenizer.pkl is absent, so a fresh
# checkout will silently build a different one from 8 shards. scripts/eet_p02_tests.sh
# has a preflight that catches a stub vocabulary, but not a differently-trained one.
tokenizer/
